WEBVTT

00:00:05.265 --> 00:00:06.865
ANNOUNCER ON PA:
That old, tired laptop

00:00:06.945 --> 00:00:09.105
moving at a sloth speed?
Bid on a new one today!

00:00:09.265 --> 00:00:11.225
SPAMLEY: Do you wanna get rich
playing video games?

00:00:11.305 --> 00:00:12.345
Click here to...

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.585
Oh. Ralph. Ralph! Hey, there.

00:00:14.745 --> 00:00:15.745
Oh, hey, Spamley.

00:00:15.825 --> 00:00:16.985
What's the good word, brother?

00:00:17.145 --> 00:00:19.425
Well, the good word is I just
paid for the steering wheel...

00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:21.025
and we are going home.

00:00:21.105 --> 00:00:22.105
Congratulations.

00:00:22.185 --> 00:00:23.345
Thanks.

00:00:23.505 --> 00:00:25.265
Hey, have you seen
Vanellope anywhere?

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:27.545
Oh, uh, your little chum?
Uh, no, no, I haven't.

00:00:27.705 --> 00:00:29.265
Hope she's not lost.

00:00:29.745 --> 00:00:31.865
Let me try to reach her
on this doohickey.

00:00:34.545 --> 00:00:35.985
(CELL PHONE VIBRATING)

00:00:39.745 --> 00:00:41.665
(INAUDIBLE)

00:00:42.185 --> 00:00:43.985
See over there?
Over that mountain?

00:00:44.065 --> 00:00:46.145
-VANELLOPE: Yeah.
-That's the Sequoia Speedway.

00:00:46.305 --> 00:00:47.785
It's gonna be unlocked
next month.

00:00:47.945 --> 00:00:49.785
Hey, what are you doing
in that awful game with her?

00:00:49.945 --> 00:00:51.305
I think the track will end...

00:00:51.465 --> 00:00:53.745
right over there.
Yo, it's gonna be so tight.

00:00:54.065 --> 00:00:55.825
-VANELLOPE: Oh, I love it.
-(INAUDIBLE)

00:00:56.105 --> 00:00:57.545
Hey, can I tell you something

00:00:57.625 --> 00:00:59.705
that I don't think
I could ever tell Ralph?

00:00:59.865 --> 00:01:00.905
SHANK: Of course.

00:01:01.065 --> 00:01:02.465
VANELLOPE:
I know it sounds crazy...

00:01:02.625 --> 00:01:06.345
but the second I walked
into this game, it felt...

00:01:07.185 --> 00:01:09.025
Well, it felt like home.

00:01:09.185 --> 00:01:11.585
I mean, more than
Sugar Rush ever did.

00:01:11.745 --> 00:01:13.585
Oh, yeah? How so?

00:01:13.745 --> 00:01:15.425
'Cause it's like my dream.

00:01:15.585 --> 00:01:17.625
It's full of weirdos...

00:01:17.785 --> 00:01:20.785
and the racing
is super dangerous...

00:01:20.985 --> 00:01:23.705
and you never know
what's gonna happen next.

00:01:24.385 --> 00:01:25.385
I mean, back home,

00:01:25.465 --> 00:01:27.745
I know exactly
what's gonna happen next...

00:01:27.945 --> 00:01:31.145
because Ralph's dream is to
do the same thing every day.

00:01:33.305 --> 00:01:34.425
Hmm.

00:01:36.465 --> 00:01:39.825
Here's something
I wish I'd learned years ago.

00:01:39.985 --> 00:01:41.585
There is no law

00:01:41.665 --> 00:01:45.105
saying best friends
have to have the same dreams.

00:01:45.265 --> 00:01:46.305
You know?

00:01:46.745 --> 00:01:47.785
Whoa.

00:01:47.865 --> 00:01:49.185
Yeah.

00:01:49.545 --> 00:01:52.745
You are a very wise person,
Shank.

00:01:52.905 --> 00:01:55.105
And a good friend, too.

00:01:55.305 --> 00:01:56.305
Thank you.

00:01:56.465 --> 00:01:58.945
Around here, peeps like to
say, "Shank you."

00:01:59.065 --> 00:02:00.145
(CHUCKLES)

00:02:00.545 --> 00:02:02.385
You know, after you go home

00:02:02.465 --> 00:02:04.225
and your life
gets back to normal...

00:02:04.385 --> 00:02:05.985
you are always welcome here.

00:02:06.145 --> 00:02:09.185
But that's the thing,
I want this to be my normal.

00:02:09.345 --> 00:02:11.425
I want this to be my life.

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:13.825
I can't go home now.

00:02:15.665 --> 00:02:17.105
I just can't.

00:02:20.105 --> 00:02:21.225
(BEEPS)

00:02:25.225 --> 00:02:26.225
Wow.

00:02:27.065 --> 00:02:28.065
You know, where I come from,

00:02:28.145 --> 00:02:30.505
that's called
a kick in the face.

00:02:30.665 --> 00:02:32.065
I can't believe it.

00:02:32.425 --> 00:02:34.945
A straight-up donkey kick
to the teeth.

00:02:35.385 --> 00:02:37.585
She's supposed to be
my best friend.

00:02:38.265 --> 00:02:39.825
No, this can't be right.

00:02:40.945 --> 00:02:42.625
No, she's been brainwashed.

00:02:42.785 --> 00:02:43.905
That's what this is.

00:02:44.105 --> 00:02:45.065
Because the Vanellope I know

00:02:45.145 --> 00:02:46.585
would never abandon me
like that.

00:02:46.745 --> 00:02:48.345
I gotta get her out
of there now.

00:02:48.505 --> 00:02:50.625
Hey, easy now, tiger.

00:02:50.825 --> 00:02:51.945
I admire the impulse...

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:54.105
but you charge in there
like some white knight...

00:02:54.265 --> 00:02:55.825
she's liable to hold it
against you.

00:02:55.985 --> 00:02:58.105
So what? I'm supposed to
just let her stay in a game

00:02:58.185 --> 00:02:59.345
that's obviously bad for her?

00:02:59.505 --> 00:03:00.585
Of course not.

00:03:00.745 --> 00:03:02.305
Then how do I make her leave?

00:03:02.465 --> 00:03:05.425
She thinks it's so cool
and exciting in there.

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:08.745
Unless you know how I can
make the game boring or...

00:03:09.465 --> 00:03:12.825
Wait. You know about viruses
and stuff, right, Spamley?

00:03:13.465 --> 00:03:15.105
-Who's asking?
-Whoa.

00:03:15.185 --> 00:03:16.665
Back home, me and the kid

00:03:16.745 --> 00:03:18.985
used to goof off
in this game called Tron.

00:03:19.185 --> 00:03:21.545
But then it got a virus that
made the motorbikes go slow...

00:03:21.705 --> 00:03:23.745
and then Vanellope stopped
wanting to hang out in there.

00:03:23.905 --> 00:03:25.305
So, is there a way

00:03:25.385 --> 00:03:27.585
to do something
like that to Slaughter Race?

00:03:27.745 --> 00:03:29.025
Oh, there's ways.

00:03:30.065 --> 00:03:31.225
Follow me.

00:03:36.025 --> 00:03:37.425
I got mothers' maiden names...

00:03:37.585 --> 00:03:39.785
social security numbers,
PIN numbers...

00:03:39.945 --> 00:03:41.105
SPAMLEY:
Now, this area down here

00:03:41.185 --> 00:03:42.585
is what's called the Darknet.

00:03:42.745 --> 00:03:44.665
A lot of shady characters
hang out down here...

00:03:44.825 --> 00:03:46.905
so try to keep a low profile.
Gord!

00:03:46.985 --> 00:03:48.385
-(YELPS)
-Oh, there you are.

00:03:48.585 --> 00:03:50.945
Now Gord here,
he's dabbled in virus-making.

00:03:51.105 --> 00:03:52.945
But his cousin,
this guy we're gonna go see...

00:03:53.105 --> 00:03:56.305
Double Dan, this dude
is a virus-making machine.

00:03:57.265 --> 00:03:58.345
Oh, oh, here we go.

00:03:58.505 --> 00:04:00.185
Are you sure this is safe?

00:04:00.345 --> 00:04:01.985
(CHUCKLES) Is it safe?
Of course it is.

00:04:02.185 --> 00:04:05.065
Just whatever you do, do not
look at his little brother.

00:04:05.145 --> 00:04:07.065
Oh, he has a little brother?

00:04:10.585 --> 00:04:12.185
Double Dan!
(CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)

00:04:12.265 --> 00:04:13.665
Long time no see.

00:04:13.865 --> 00:04:14.985
Who are you?

00:04:15.145 --> 00:04:16.145
(STAMMERS) JP Spamley.

00:04:16.545 --> 00:04:18.385
Uh, we met one time
over at Friendster...

00:04:18.545 --> 00:04:21.705
which tells you
it had to be a long time ago.

00:04:22.185 --> 00:04:23.785
-Oye. What are you looking at?
-Nothing.

00:04:23.865 --> 00:04:24.865
Are you looking at my brother?

00:04:24.945 --> 00:04:25.945
-No, sir.
-Don't you look

00:04:26.025 --> 00:04:27.025
at my little brother.

00:04:27.105 --> 00:04:29.225
-Oh, no, I wasn't.
-He's very self-conscious!

00:04:29.305 --> 00:04:30.385
(GROANS)

00:04:30.505 --> 00:04:31.985
-(GROWLS)
-(GASPS)

00:04:32.385 --> 00:04:33.465
You?

00:04:33.625 --> 00:04:35.185
What are you doing here?

00:04:35.265 --> 00:04:36.465
Uh... (CLEARS THROAT)

00:04:36.545 --> 00:04:38.625
The reason I came to
your neck of the face...

00:04:38.785 --> 00:04:41.425
I mean, there's a face
in your neck. I mean, woods.

00:04:41.585 --> 00:04:43.945
Neck of the woods. The reason
I'm here is 'cause I...

00:04:44.145 --> 00:04:46.225
Well, I heard a little tumor,
rumor...

00:04:46.385 --> 00:04:47.905
I heard a rumor
that you could, well,

00:04:48.025 --> 00:04:50.065
give me a harmless virus
kind of thing...

00:04:50.225 --> 00:04:51.305
that might be able to

00:04:51.385 --> 00:04:53.225
slow down
the Slaughter Race game?

00:04:53.385 --> 00:04:54.585
Oh, yeah.

00:04:55.145 --> 00:04:57.905
My cousin Gordon told me
that you wanted to crash it.

00:04:57.985 --> 00:04:58.985
Crash it? No!

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:00.785
No, no, no.

00:05:00.945 --> 00:05:02.425
(STAMMERS) I don't want
anyone getting hurt.

00:05:02.505 --> 00:05:03.585
DOUBLE DAN: Hmm.

00:05:03.665 --> 00:05:05.585
If there's a way to just,
uh...

00:05:05.745 --> 00:05:06.785
I don't know...

00:05:06.865 --> 00:05:08.865
just make the cars
go slow or something...

00:05:09.025 --> 00:05:11.265
so the game is boring...

00:05:11.465 --> 00:05:13.185
and my friend
comes back home to me.

00:05:13.585 --> 00:05:17.425
Allow me to
introduce you to Arthur.

00:05:17.505 --> 00:05:18.945
-(GROWLING)
-(BOTH YELPING)

00:05:19.025 --> 00:05:20.785
Easy there, boy. (LAUGHS)

00:05:21.065 --> 00:05:22.545
He's keen.

00:05:22.705 --> 00:05:26.385
Arthur's what I call
an insecurity virus.

00:05:26.545 --> 00:05:29.505
Means he looks for
little flaws and weaknesses

00:05:29.585 --> 00:05:31.505
that make a program insecure.

00:05:34.025 --> 00:05:36.705
You release him
into that Slaughter Race game,

00:05:36.785 --> 00:05:39.345
Arthur will find some defect
in the code.

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:41.025
Then he'll copy that defect

00:05:41.105 --> 00:05:43.465
and spread it
all over the game...

00:05:43.665 --> 00:05:47.305
until everything becomes,
quote, unquote, "boring"...

00:05:47.505 --> 00:05:49.745
just like you wanted.

00:05:49.905 --> 00:05:50.905
Okay.

00:05:51.065 --> 00:05:52.825
Just to be super clear here...

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:54.265
no one gets hurt, right?

00:05:54.465 --> 00:05:55.505
Are you stupid?

00:05:55.585 --> 00:05:56.585
Well, uh...

00:05:56.745 --> 00:05:58.785
Because the only way
anyone gets hurt...

00:05:58.945 --> 00:06:00.305
is if you are stupid.

00:06:00.465 --> 00:06:01.585
All you have to do...

00:06:01.745 --> 00:06:05.105
is make sure the virus stays
in Slaughter Race.

00:06:05.305 --> 00:06:07.145
Right. Don't be stupid.

00:06:07.305 --> 00:06:08.745
Make sure it doesn't get out
of Slaughter Race.

00:06:08.825 --> 00:06:09.825
Goiter it. Gah!

00:06:09.905 --> 00:06:10.945
-Got it! Got it.
-Get out!

00:06:11.105 --> 00:06:12.265
Thank you, you're a cyst face.

00:06:12.425 --> 00:06:13.625
-Out!
-I mean, assistance.

00:06:13.785 --> 00:06:15.505
Thank you for your
cyst face... Assistance.

00:06:15.665 --> 00:06:17.065
-Get out!
-RALPH: Goodbye!

00:06:17.145 --> 00:06:18.345
Ugh.

00:06:18.705 --> 00:06:20.945
(PYRO PANTING)

00:06:21.665 --> 00:06:23.505
Ah! Fiddlesticks!
Well, that's game.

00:06:23.665 --> 00:06:24.865
Ah, beginner's luck.

00:06:25.025 --> 00:06:26.625
Come on, kid.
I know a hustle

00:06:26.705 --> 00:06:27.705
-when I see one.
-(CHUCKLES)

00:06:27.785 --> 00:06:28.825
(HORN BLARES)

00:06:28.905 --> 00:06:30.545
-Player's on the way.
-Thanks, Bob.

00:06:30.705 --> 00:06:32.105
-Let's roll!
-PYRO: Game faces on, guys.

00:06:32.265 --> 00:06:34.505
Show time.
You ready for your first race?

00:06:34.585 --> 00:06:36.625
Um, yeah. I think so.

00:06:36.785 --> 00:06:39.265
Hey, don't be nervous.
You're gonna be great.

00:06:39.425 --> 00:06:41.505
Yeah, no, I know.
I'll be fine.

00:06:41.585 --> 00:06:44.065
Mmm. You didn't tell
Ralph yet, did you?

00:06:45.025 --> 00:06:46.705
Not exactly.

00:06:46.865 --> 00:06:49.345
Come on, V.
He's your best friend.

00:06:49.505 --> 00:06:50.505
You gotta let him know

00:06:50.585 --> 00:06:52.185
you're planning on
staying here for a while.

00:06:52.345 --> 00:06:55.185
I know. But he's gonna
get really upset.

00:06:55.345 --> 00:06:57.185
Yeah, he might,
but you guys...

00:06:57.345 --> 00:06:59.985
you'll talk, you'll work it
out, you'll figure it out.

00:07:00.145 --> 00:07:01.745
Yeah, but what if we don't?

00:07:01.945 --> 00:07:04.385
What if his feelings
get hurt so bad...

00:07:04.545 --> 00:07:06.625
he won't wanna be
my friend anymore?

00:07:06.825 --> 00:07:09.905
Look.
All friendships change...

00:07:10.065 --> 00:07:11.225
but the good ones...

00:07:11.705 --> 00:07:13.145
they get stronger
because of it.

00:07:13.225 --> 00:07:14.305
(HORN BLARES)

00:07:14.505 --> 00:07:16.225
Uh, Shank,
I hate to bother you...

00:07:16.385 --> 00:07:18.585
but the player is waiting.

00:07:18.745 --> 00:07:20.625
I'm not gonna tell you
what to do, kid.

00:07:20.785 --> 00:07:22.065
It's your call.

00:07:22.705 --> 00:07:23.745
Yeah, okay.

00:07:24.665 --> 00:07:25.665
(SIGHS) All right.

00:07:25.745 --> 00:07:26.905
Let's race.

00:07:30.465 --> 00:07:31.505
(SIGHS)

00:07:33.145 --> 00:07:34.945
(ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)

00:07:41.185 --> 00:07:43.425
ARTHUR:
Scanning for insecurities.

00:07:45.585 --> 00:07:47.465
Scanning for insecurities.

00:07:49.665 --> 00:07:51.665
ANNOUNCER: "Precious Car-go."

00:07:51.825 --> 00:07:53.825
Deliver the car
to Bert's Chop Shop...

00:07:53.985 --> 00:07:56.705
but watch out
for Shank and her crew.

00:07:56.945 --> 00:07:59.345
(TIRES SCREECHING)

